<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p>USE OF GUIDANCE NOTES</p>
<p>Guidance Notes are issued by SSX to promote commercial certainty, to reduce regulatory and compliance costs to business and to assist market participants. &nbsp;SSX is available to discuss any questions you may have in relation to a Guidance Note, and to do so you can contact SSX at&nbsp;<a href="mailto:info@apx.com.au">info@ssx.sydney</a></p>
<p>SSX may replace Guidance Notes at any time.&nbsp; All relevant entities should contact SSX to ensure that they have the latest version of a Guidance Note.&nbsp; As a Guidance Note is only a guide to SSX policy, practice and interpretation, entities are advised to contact SSX to discuss their particular circumstances and the resultant application of the SSX Listing Rules. SSX cannot give legal advice to entities and recommends that entities consider taking advice from a qualified professional person.</p>
</div>
